A set of elements of Pω is an enumeration degree if and only if it is the combinatory subalgebra generated by some finite list.

If the set is the degree of an element a, it equals the subalgebra generated by the singleton list of a. An element of the degree is a combinatory application to a, and the generated subalgebra contains every combinator and contains the generator a. Conversely, every element of the generated subalgebra lies in every subalgebra containing the generators, and the degree of a is such a subalgebra containing a. In the other direction, the subalgebra generated by a list equals the degree of the single generator of that list.
